    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Merge Intervals\n\nGiven an array of intervals where intervals[i] = [start_i, end_i], merge all overlapping intervals and return an array of the non-overlapping intervals that cover all the intervals in the input.\n\nExample: [[1,3],[2,6],[8,10],[15,18]] -> [[1,6],[8,10],[15,18]].\nConstraints: 1 <= len(intervals) <= 10^4.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-01T01:26:25.294Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Constraints are small enough that the obvious approach fits, but the follow-up asks for the optimal one; going straight to it.\n\nComplexity check: one pass, O(n) time, O(n) auxiliary space for the map. That meets the constraint.\n\nEdge cases to cover before submitting: empty input, single element, and the all-duplicates case.",
      "id": "m-2",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-01T01:26:25.506Z",
      "durationMs": 3843,
      "stepIndex": 1
    },
